<!--
  RM_Vorrel.xml                             LONGSHADE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 step 2

  Moved and renamed from src/RimUtinni/AshkarrFlora/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/
  RUT_Staggerseed.xml (RUT_Vorrel -> RM_Vorrel), per biome_mod_architecture.md
  §7 Q8: dissolve ashkarrflora's per-biome content, plants move into the
  biome's own RM mod, renamed RM_. Content below is otherwise unchanged from
  that file — full authoring history (DESERT_STAGGERSEED_BUILD_1, the ban
  checks, the art-search record) stays there in git history, not repeated here.

  The desert's cycle plant. FROZEN sheet:
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/desert.md (BIOME_FREEZE_FABLE_REVIEW_1),
  §4b "The seed that uses you" and §7 "Uniquely available".

    "An edible-looking plant of the protected water pockets whose fruit,
    eaten raw, hatches its seeds inside your belly. It kills quickly, and
    the dying animal does what every dying animal here does: staggers
    toward the next shade — and dies in it. The seeds germinate there, in
    the one place they could not otherwise reach." ... "It disperses by
    killing, and it aims at shade." ... "And the seeds are a delicacy.
    Prepared correctly, the preparation lets them begin to grow and then
    perish before they can hurt you — producing euphoria."

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED. §4b marks it "(Name owner's pick. Working:
  vorrel.)" — the ultracactus's name already stands, this one's does
  not. `RM_Vorrel` is the INTERNAL working defName and every label below is
  provisional; the owner card is items/closed/STAGGERSEED_SHIPPING_NAME_1.md
  and DESERT_STAGGERSEED_BUILD_1 stays open until it returns. Renaming is
  five files and one wildPlants line, same as before the move.

  THE THREE DESERT PLANTS SORT BY FERTILITY, and that is the player's
  water-table instrument (the ruling behind it is SURRA_GRASS_FERTILITYMIN_1,
  owner 2026-09-20: fertilityMin confines a plant on purpose, and green means
  water). RSW_Ultracactus 0.05 — open sand nobody else uses. RSW_SurraGrass
  (surra grass) 0.30 — the dew-line halo around soil islands. This plant
  0.45 — the "protected water pockets" themselves, the tightest niche of the
  three. Core Sand is fertility 0.10, so this can never take sand.

  Ban check against §6: ban 1 (nothing keyed to time of day) — nothing here
  reads glow or hour; the mechanic keys to SHADE, which is the sheet's own
  substitute. Ban 5 (no local fire ecology) — Flammability 0, same as the
  ultracactus. Ban 8 (no lush) — visualSizeRange caps at 0.8 and the wild
  cluster is small and rare; this is never a green mass.

  ART: no art has been generated for this plant under either name (checked
  infrastructure/artpipe/{done,_artsrc,registry.jsonl} for "vorrel" at the
  2026-09-24 move — zero hits under that name; two DONE jobs exist under the
  OLD job names rutstaggerseed_v1/rutstaggerseeddish_v1,
  infrastructure/artpipe/done/rutstaggerseed_v1.manifest.json +
  rutstaggerseeddish_v1.manifest.json, rendered PNGs in
  infrastructure/artpipe/_artsrc/rutstaggerseed_v1/ +
  rutstaggerseeddish_v1/ — but never deployed to a Textures/ folder under
  either the old or the new texPath. Not this pass's scope to deploy; flagged
  in the build report). texPaths below point at this mod's own Textures/,
  unchanged in shape from the old ones (RUT_Vorrel -> RM_Vorrel).

  🔑 The art brief's own hard requirement, which is a DESIGN constraint and
  not a style note: the bush must read as harmless and appetising. §4b's word
  is "edible-looking", and a plant that telegraphed the trap would not be the
  trap.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ============== The plant ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Vorrel</defName>
    <label>vorrel</label>
    <description>A low, dense bush of the shaded water pockets, hung with fat pale fruit that looks like the most ordinary good luck on this planet. It is not. Each fruit is packed with live seed that takes root in the gut of whatever eats it, and a body full of them has hours, not days. What the plant wants from the arrangement is the walk: a dying animal here makes for the nearest shadow by instinct, and a shadow is the one ground a seed could never have reached on its own.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>110</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>0.45</Nutrition>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- Art pending deploy — see this file's header. -->
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Vorrel</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.5, 0.2, 0.2)</volume>
        <offset>(0,0,-0.25)</offset>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <neverMultiSelect>false</neverMultiSelect>
    <fillPercent>0.2</fillPercent>
    <pathCost>20</pathCost>

    <!-- The trap, and the reason it is on the PLANT and not only on the
         harvested fruit: Verse/Thing.cs Ingested runs def.ingestible.
         outcomeDoers for whatever is being eaten, and a grazing animal eats
         the PLANT, never the harvested item. MEASURED from the decompiled
         engine (unchanged from before the move). Put the brood only on the
         fruit and the entire corpse-dispersal cycle would exist on paper and
         never once fire in a wild biome, because nothing wild harvests.
         Colonists get it from either route: browsing the bush raw, or eating
         the raw fruit. -->
    <ingestible>
      <foodType>VegetableOrFruit</foodType>
      <preferability>RawTasty</preferability>
      <outcomeDoers>
        <li Class="IngestionOutcomeDoer_GiveHediff">
          <hediffDef>RM_VorrelBrood</hediffDef>
          <severity>0.1</severity>
        </li>
      </outcomeDoers>
    </ingestible>

    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.45</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.5</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>9</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
      <maxMeshCount>4</maxMeshCount>
      <visualSizeRange>0.5~0.8</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.2</topWindExposure>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <harvestedThingDef>RM_VorrelFruit</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>6</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>220</harvestWork>
      <harvestAfterGrowth>0.4</harvestAfterGrowth>
      <wildClusterRadius>4</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>30</wildClusterWeight>
      <wildOrder>2</wildOrder>
      <purpose>Food</purpose>
      <humanFoodPlant>true</humanFoodPlant>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
